                                "text": "1831-1850, William Youatt, On the Structure and the Diseases of the Horse\nAnother species of blindness , and of which mention was made when describing the retina , is Gutta Serena , commonly called glass eye. The pupil is more than usually dilated : it is immovable , and bright , and glassy ."
